A||||4||WisconsinGT||Pinging question.||||1||
Z||000000||WisconsinGT||06-21-2000||12:36 AM||||My 88 2.8 GT seems to ping (Sounds like a bunch of marbles in the engine) only when I am going up a hill under acceleration. Would anyone have any idea what it could be or where I should look? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||06-21-2000||12:51 AM||||First guess is the EGR passage is clogged or the EGR is stuck closed.<P>Does it do it worse at part throttle?||||reg||1
Z||000002||ROB MAC||06-21-2000||01:17 AM||||If the EGR and the timing are O.K. try some higher octane gas.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||06-21-2000||02:17 AM||||EGR stuck closed won't cause pinging unless your timing is set too retarded. If Timing is too far advanced you'll get pinging. Bad gas can cause pinging. (rumor has it some evil gas stations are filling tanks with 87 octane but dispensing it as 93 octane and charging the higher price!) Do you have any ECM codes stored? My suggestion is check codes if clear, check timing, Then try EGR and some gas treatment.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||06-21-2000||09:37 AM||||Had the same problem with my 88 3.1 engine.  I tried everything.  Especially loud pinging goining up long hills.  I retarded the timing, used 93 octane, new wires, plugs, ignition coil, egr seninoid, on and on.<P>It's in for a 3.4 engine transplant.<P>Twin Lakes has the car and the engine is out.  Only 15 K miles on the engine, synthetic oil every 3K miles.  Maybe I gave up too easy.||||reg||1
